1
00:00:01,104 --> 00:00:08,211
Last summer, my cousin Yui flew in from Osaka, to spend a week at Uncle Pedro's farm in the south of Spain.

2
00:00:08,726 --> 00:00:11,421
Yui had four years of English in school.

3
00:00:11,122 --> 00:00:12,749
Spain was going to test all of it.

4
00:00:14,628 --> 00:00:16,718
The cow is the queen of the house!

5
00:00:17,838 --> 00:00:21,497
Uncle Pedro had one rule about his cow, Luna.

6
00:00:21,198 --> 00:00:22,473
You may look.

7
00:00:22,174 --> 00:00:23,632
You may pet.

8
00:00:23,333 --> 00:00:25,223
But you never joke about the cow.

9
00:00:27,028 --> 00:00:29,163
And she's the cleverest cow in town!

10
00:00:32,106 --> 00:00:34,610
In Japanese, baka means stupid.

11
00:00:34,311 --> 00:00:36,479
In Spanish, vaca means cow.

12
00:00:36,996 --> 00:00:42,035
Say them fast, and Uncle Pedro had just called the queen an idiot.

13
00:00:41,736 --> 00:00:42,924
Three times.

14
00:00:44,756 --> 00:00:45,930
Hang in there.

15
00:00:47,702 --> 00:00:50,240
That's it! Vaca!

16
00:00:51,364 --> 00:00:52,658
I'm so sorry.

17
00:00:56,472 --> 00:00:57,683
​Vaca.

18
00:00:57,384 --> 00:00:58,425
Cow.

19
00:00:58,126 --> 00:00:59,131
Not baka.

20
00:01:01,502 --> 00:01:04,269
See? She agrees.

21
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:08,383
Come on! To my house!

22
00:01:09,898 --> 00:01:11,104
My… cow?

23
00:01:12,972 --> 00:01:17,672
That evening, Uncle Pedro painted MIKASA over her stable.

24
00:01:17,373 --> 00:01:20,018
He thinks it's Japanese for 'the queen's house.'

25
00:01:20,590 --> 00:01:22,404
Nobody corrected him.

26
00:01:22,105 --> 00:01:23,779
The cow answers to it now.
